    "findings": [
      "Reviewed all seven Quickloader formal pages and the current 1-trait/3-binding mapping; the player page, three actual autogun marks, shared map, and weapon reverse index agree.",
      "I–IV are +10%, +12.5%, +15%, and +20% reload speed for 2 seconds. A processed dodge-start event while the applicable slot is wielded is sufficient; no successful dodge, shot, or hit is required. Repeated eligible events refresh the window without stacking or cooldown.",
      "The tier reload_speed override replaces the ProcBuff 0.5 fallback while active; it is not added to that value or permanently applied. The applicable held gate is enforced on proc-stat contribution.",
      "Reload action time scale is sampled when a reload starts. The 10-second example yields 8.33 seconds at IV and a 16.67% duration reduction under its stated unclamped, no-other-bonus assumptions; it does not claim a fixed mark reload duration.",
      "The RAW keys and paired resource hash match. All four EN/ZH static reconstructions use the formatter values and 2-second duration; the text correctly treats event-start versus successful-dodge wording as unspecified by RAW.",
      "The Quickloader image exception is accurately limited to this item: original icon, icon_small, and mastery_icon are empty in the identified public metadata snapshot; the formal catalogs say no verifiable icon, with no substitute attachment or image-verification claim."
    ],
